  "pylon_limitations": {
    "primary_known": "Rigid mounting, total Ww, chordwise CG offset ew and polar inertia Iw about wing EA. Weight7 variants obtained by moving same weight along support; table gives slightly different whole added weights.",
    "primary_missing": "No dimensioned pylon/weight drawing or complete three-dimensional CG and centroidal inertia tensor; photographs do not establish transverse/axial offsets or bending rotary inertia.",
    "support_mass": "TableI names concentrated weight parameters, and text describes moving weight on weight support. Treat each tabulated set as measured aggregate added assembly for the equivalent model; report does not separately quantify support mass. Do not add a guessed pylon mass on top.",
    "two_point_equivalence": "Two equal point masses along chord at same station match total mass, chordwise CG and spanwise polar inertia only. They invent zero normal/axial extent and corresponding bending inertia; finite object geometry cannot be inferred from this reduction.",
    "literal_axial_offset": "The ASW parameter starts at0.0001 while physical z starts0. A listed t=z therefore has dz=z-s=0.0001*(L-t)/(L-0.0001). This is under0.1mm and zero at tip; it is due to parameterization, not primary pylon geometry.",
    "sources": "TN1594 printed p.4 / PDF p.5; TableI printed p.8 / PDF p.9; Figure3(g) printed p.25 / PDF p.26",
    "spanwise_station_ambiguity": "TableII header says Spanwise position (in. from root); text does not explicitly identify assembly CG versus attachment. Co-location of equivalent mass CG and attachment at the tabulated station is a reduced-model assumption."
  },
  "gravity": {
    "direction": "Vertical wing clamped at tunnel top, tip downward; gravity positive root-to-tip. In literal geometry with root z0 and tip z+1.2192, use gravity (0,0,+g). Do not impose default -z without rotating model.",
    "preload": "Axial tension N(s)=g[m(L-s)+sum(Mp for points outboard of s)] for centered straight idealization. Chordwise CG offsets also produce in-plane gravity moments; literal model suppresses in-plane bending with its stiff limit. Physically correct full equilibrium needs unreported in-plane stiffness or an explicit stiff in-plane approximation.",
    "zero_gravity_status": "Numerical implementation control only, not physical experimental state.",
    "g_value": "Primary does not report local g; standard9.80665m/s2 or literal9.81 is a documented convention with0.034% difference.",
    "source": "TN1594 printed pp.3-4 / PDF pp.4-5 and Figure1 printed p.15 / PDF p.16"
  },
  "measurement_medium": {
    "no_flow": "TableII zero-speed before/after frequency rows list0% Freon12. Thus air surrounds the wing; no zero-pressure/vacuum measurement is reported.",
    "density": "Density entries on the zero-speed rows are blank. Temperature, pressure and density for those measurements are not specified. The apparatus could vary absolute pressure from30 to4.3inHg; therefore0%Freon does not prove sea-level density.",
    "standard_air_entry": "TN1594 properties list 1/kappa=32.6 for standard air,no weight as a reference parameter, not a record of all zero-flow test densities.",
    "flutter_conditions": "Flutter rows record density, and some early runs use Freon/air mixtures. Do not substitute a flutter-row density or imported rho_SL for no-flow density without saying it is an assumption.",
    "endplate": "Report says endplate effect on natural frequencies negligible (printed p.7/PDF p.8), though flutter behavior differs. Small disturbance aerodynamic added mass remains even at zero mean speed; any modeled operator and ambient density require explicit assumptions.",
    "sources": "TN1594 TableII printed pp.9-13 / PDF pp.10-14 visually reviewed; apparatus printed p.3 / PDF p.4; test procedure printed p.5 / PDF p.6; endplate frequency statement printed p.7 / PDF p.8"
  },
  "uncertainty": "Report gives printed precision and repeated before/after measurements, but no calibrated uncertainty for mass/stiffness/inertia or modal estimates. Treat before/after spread as observed repeat/change evidence, not a confidence interval. No frequency fitting performed.",
